target: internal/push/push.go
verify: go test ./internal/push/ -count=1 -run 'TestCheckDiagnosesARunMissingFromTheStore'
expect: it must stay silent
why:    the GREEN half of the guard above. Named for every CHECK, not every refusal: the anchor is the `if r == nil` block, which sits BEFORE the reportProbe branch, so making it unconditional fires the note on every call, refusals about the report included — unlike the sibling `push-diag-written-on-every-refusal`, whose anchor really is inside the refusal branch. The two names used to read identically and mean different things. A note that fires on every call is not a signal: the whole value of the line is that its PRESENCE distinguishes a wrong -store from a report that was simply never posted. Over-firing is a failure mode, not a safe default — this repo's learnings require both directions of a guard to be validated, and the RED side alone is satisfied by a note that is always on. Here the run IS in the store and the refusal IS about the report, so the note must not appear.
--- old
	if r == nil {
		r = &record.Run{ID: p.RunID}
		if p.Diag != nil {
--- new
	if true {
		if r == nil {
			r = &record.Run{ID: p.RunID}
		}
		if p.Diag != nil {
